  "_comment": "CLICK TRAINER — scene definition on the NEW system (201F4F51): behaviour + a template-FREE arrangement tree of primitive component KINDS + exits. The `clicktrainer` behaviour (registered by the client) plays it: the Rust game (2D sprite target + lifetime bar + hit/miss scoring + difficulty ramp) draws UNDER this vector HUD, and the walker reports `hud_hit` so a click on the panel is a UI click (RESET), never a game miss. Stat values flow from the behaviour via Model as pre-formatted text (`text_bind`). Esc fires the declared `on_menu = pause_open` intent → the behaviour pushes the shared pause popup, exactly like Populous. No protos, no expand — this is the reference second adopter of the post-template pattern.",
